spec: S14-02

`skill install` in a sandbox: the default location `./.agents/skills/annotary/SKILL.md` (dirs
created, the path printed, a note about `--dir`), a second run is `unchanged`, a differing file
is refused without `--force` (exit 5) and overwritten with it, `--dir DIR` lands in
`DIR/annotary/SKILL.md`, `--json` bare / `?`. Needs no server or credential. (Byte equality
with the embedded skill and `metadata.version` == `--version` are asserted by
`crates/annotary/tests/cli_skill.rs`.) Merged stdout+stderr.

```console
$ annotary skill install
wrote ./.agents/skills/annotary/SKILL.md (v0.0.0)
also: --dir ~/.claude/skills (any skills dir — the file lands in DIR/annotary/SKILL.md)

$ annotary skill install
unchanged ./.agents/skills/annotary/SKILL.md (v0.0.0)
also: --dir ~/.claude/skills (any skills dir — the file lands in DIR/annotary/SKILL.md)

$ annotary skill install -q
unchanged ./.agents/skills/annotary/SKILL.md (v0.0.0)

$ sh edit.sh

$ annotary skill install
? 5
error: ./.agents/skills/annotary/SKILL.md exists and differs from the embedded v0.0.0 (edited?) — `--force` overwrites it

$ annotary skill install --force --json
{"path":"./.agents/skills/annotary/SKILL.md","version":"0.0.0","written":true}

$ annotary skill install --dir skills --json
{"path":"skills/annotary/SKILL.md","version":"0.0.0","written":true}

$ annotary skill install --dir skills
unchanged skills/annotary/SKILL.md (v0.0.0)

$ annotary skill install --json ?
path version written dir previous

```
